Statutory Authority: The Delhi Police Act, 1978
Provision Reference: Section 28
Statutory Text:
28. Power to make regulations for regulating traffic and for preservation of order in public place, etc.—
(1) The Commissioner of Police may, by notification in the Official Gazette, make regulations to provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:—
(a) licensing and controlling persons offering themselves for employment at quays, wharves and landing places, and the licensing and controlling plying of boats;
(b) regulating traffic of all kinds in streets and other public places and the use of streets and other public places by persons riding, driving, cycling, walking or accompanying any animal;
(f) regulating music or other sound in public places;
(o) licensing or controlling places of public amusement or public entertainment.

